# pnpm's default (isolated) linker plus a total public hoist.
#
# Two constraints pull in opposite directions, and this is the only combination
# found that satisfies both.
#
#   maximal-core's build refuses to run without a package-local node_modules --
#   `bun build` writes module paths relative to the resolved build root, so a
#   bundle built without one is not byte-comparable. `node-linker=hoisted`
#   empties every package-local tree, so it is out.
#
#   Electron Forge refuses to run under pnpm unless node-linker is hoisted OR a
#   hoist pattern is defined. Separately, Vite 8's Rolldown resolves a
#   symlinked package's imports from the symlink path rather than the realpath,
#   so Radix's transitive deps (@radix-ui/react-primitive, react-remove-scroll)
#   are invisible under isolated linking and the renderer build fails one
#   package at a time as each is hoisted by hand.
#
# `public-hoist-pattern[]=*` resolves both: everything is also placed in the
# root node_modules, so symlink-path resolution finds it, and Forge sees a
# hoist pattern -- while the isolated linker still gives every package its own
# node_modules. With this, `electron-forge package` produces a working
# Maximal.app.
#
# The cost: a total public hoist re-hides undeclared dependencies, which is
# exactly how the typebox / @types/node / @electron/packager phantoms stayed
# invisible upstream. All three are declared properly here (see SOURCES.md), but
# this setting means the workspace will no longer catch the next one. An install
# with this line removed is the way to check for new phantoms.
public-hoist-pattern[]=*
